course: dictionary
lesson: 7715
title: One word, two meanings: pub
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pub is a place where adults buy and drink beer and other drinks, and often eat meals. Pub is short for «public house». You can find pubs in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand.
explain: Read the words around the word. «Theatre happens anywhere, from a huge London theatre to a tiny room above a pub.» The sentence tells you a pub is a building, because a room can be above it. Can you see the clue?
explain: Sometimes «pub» means something different. If a friend says, «Let's go to the pub tonight», she probably means going out to meet friends for a drink, not the building itself. Ask yourself: does the sentence make sense if I swap in my meaning?
fact: A pub is a place where adults buy and drink beer and other drinks, and often eat meals.
fact: Pub is short for «public house».
fact: Pubs are found in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: «A pub is a place where adults meet, talk, sometimes eat and usually drink beer.»
fact: Children can only go into a pub with adults, and they cannot buy alcohol.
exercise: In «Theatre happens anywhere, from a huge London theatre to a tiny room above a pub», what kind of place is a pub? | *A place where adults buy and drink beer and other drinks | A school for young children | A huge London theatre | A hospital for animals
exercise: Pub is short for which two words? | *public house | play house | private room | pub lunch
exercise: Your friend says, «Let's go to the pub tonight.» What does this most likely mean? | Going to bed early | *Going out to meet friends for a drink | Going to a hospital for a check-up | Going inside a theatre to watch a show
test: In «Cigarettes... smoking is banned inside workplaces and pubs, so smokers go outside even in the rain», why do smokers go outside? | Because they want to get wet | Because the pubs are closed in the rain | Because pubs are too small for a crowd | *Because smoking is banned inside pubs and workplaces
test: Which country is listed as a place where pubs are found? | *New Zealand | Egypt | Brazil | Canada
exam: In «Afterwards there is often a wake, sandwiches and cake at a pub or a hall», what does pub mean? | *A place where adults buy and drink beer and other drinks, and often eat meals | A shop that sells shoes | A small theatre for children | A kind of sandwich
